<body>
<div class="poster">

  <!-- HEADER -->
  <div class="header">
    <div class="conference">Medical AI &amp; Digital Health Conference 2024</div>
    <h1>Large Language Models in Medicine:<br>Opportunities, Risks, and the Path Forward</h1>
    <div class="subtitle">A comprehensive review of how large language models are transforming clinical practice, medical research, and healthcare delivery &mdash; along with the critical challenges that must be addressed.</div>
  </div>

  <!-- METRICS ROW -->
  <div class="metrics-row">
    <div class="metric-card navy">
      <div class="value">&gt;90%</div>
      <div class="label">GPT-4 USMLE Score</div>
      <div class="context">Exceeded passing threshold on all three steps of the USMLE</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card teal">
      <div class="value">500+</div>
      <div class="label">PubMed Articles (2023)</div>
      <div class="context">Peer-reviewed publications on LLMs in medicine in 2023 alone</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card accent">
      <div class="value">Up to 30%</div>
      <div class="label">Hallucination Rate</div>
      <div class="context">Fabricated medical references or inaccurate clinical information</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card teal">
      <div class="value">$10.5B</div>
      <div class="label">Projected Market (2030)</div>
      <div class="context">Global healthcare LLM market projected by 2030</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- CONTENT -->
  <div class="content">

    <!-- OVERVIEW + APPLICATIONS -->
    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="panel overview-panel">
        <h2>What Are LLMs and Why Do They Matter?</h2>
        <p>Large language models (LLMs) such as <strong>GPT-4</strong>, <strong>Med-PaLM 2</strong>, and <strong>LLaMA</strong> have rapidly entered the healthcare landscape, demonstrating remarkable capabilities in understanding and generating medical text.</p>
        <br>
        <p>A landmark review published in <em>Nature Medicine</em> (July 2023) examined how these foundation models &mdash; trained on vast corpora of text data &mdash; are poised to reshape clinical practice, biomedical research, and medical education.</p>
        <br>
        <p>The pace of adoption has been extraordinary: over 500 peer-reviewed publications appeared in 2023 alone, and the global healthcare LLM market is projected to reach $10.5 billion by 2030.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Key Clinical &amp; Research Applications</h2>
        <div class="app-grid">
          <div class="app-item">
            <div class="app-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8l-6-6zm-1 1.5L18.5 9H13V3.5zM6 20V4h5v7h7v9H6z"/></svg></div>
            <div class="app-body">
              <h3>Clinical Documentation</h3>
              <div class="app-desc">Automated note generation, discharge summaries</div>
              <span class="maturity">Pilot Deployments</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="app-item">
            <div class="app-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2C6.48 2 2 6.48 2 12s4.48 10 10 10 10-4.48 10-10S17.52 2 12 2zm-2 15l-5-5 1.41-1.41L10 14.17l7.59-7.59L19 8l-9 9z"/></svg></div>
            <div class="app-body">
              <h3>Diagnostic Support</h3>
              <div class="app-desc">Differential diagnosis, radiology report interpretation</div>
              <span class="maturity">Research Stage</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="app-item">
            <div class="app-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M20 2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v18l4-4h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2z"/></svg></div>
            <div class="app-body">
              <h3>Patient Communication</h3>
              <div class="app-desc">Answering questions, simplifying medical jargon</div>
              <span class="maturity">Early Adoption</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="app-item">
            <div class="app-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3L1 9l4 2.18v6L12 21l7-3.82v-6l2-1.09V17h2V9L12 3z"/></svg></div>
            <div class="app-body">
              <h3>Medical Education</h3>
              <div class="app-desc">Exam preparation, case-based learning, tutoring</div>
              <span class="maturity">Active Use</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="app-item">
            <div class="app-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9.5 2A7.5 7.5 0 0 1 17 9.5c0 1.7-.6 3.3-1.5 4.6l5.1 5.1-1.4 1.4-5.1-5.1A7.5 7.5 0 1 1 9.5 2z"/></svg></div>
            <div class="app-body">
              <h3>Biomedical Research</h3>
              <div class="app-desc">Literature synthesis, hypothesis generation, protocol drafting</div>
              <span class="maturity">Emerging</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PERFORMANCE -->
    <div class="performance-section">
      <h2>Performance Benchmarks &amp; Evidence</h2>
      <div class="perf-container">
        <div class="perf-chart-area">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 800 420" width="100%" height="100%" style="overflow:visible">
            <rect x="0" y="0" width="800" height="420" fill="#FAFBFC" rx="12"/>
            <!-- Grid lines -->
            <line x1="100" y1="50" x2="740" y2="50" stroke="#E5E7EB" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4"/>
            <line x1="100" y1="122" x2="740" y2="122" stroke="#E5E7EB" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4"/>
            <line x1="100" y1="194" x2="740" y2="194" stroke="#E5E7EB" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4"/>
            <line x1="100" y1="266" x2="740" y2="266" stroke="#E5E7EB" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4"/>
            <line x1="100" y1="338" x2="740" y2="338" stroke="#D1D5DB" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <!-- Y-axis labels -->
            <text x="90" y="55" text-anchor="end" font-size="18" fill="#6B7280" font-family="sans-serif">100%</text>
            <text x="90" y="127" text-anchor="end" font-size="18" fill="#6B7280" font-family="sans-serif">75%</text>
            <text x="90" y="199" text-anchor="end" font-size="18" fill="#6B7280" font-family="sans-serif">50%</text>
            <text x="90" y="271" text-anchor="end" font-size="18" fill="#6B7280" font-family="sans-serif">25%</text>
            <text x="90" y="343" text-anchor="end" font-size="18" fill="#6B7280" font-family="sans-serif">0%</text>
            <!-- Passing threshold line -->
            <line x1="100" y1="166" x2="740" y2="166" stroke="#D4763A" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="8,4"/>
            <text x="745" y="171" font-size="16" fill="#D4763A" font-weight="600" font-family="sans-serif">Pass ~60%</text>
            <!-- Gradients -->
            <defs>
              <linearGradient id="g1" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#9CA3AF"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#6B7280"/></linearGradient>
              <linearGradient id="g2" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#5A9BAB"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#3D7A8A"/></linearGradient>
              <linearGradient id="g3" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="#2A3F6A"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#1B2A4A"/></linearGradient>
            </defs>
            <!-- GPT-3.5 bar (~60%) -->
            <rect x="190" y="166" width="110" height="172" fill="url(#g1)" rx="6"/>
            <text x="245" y="152" text-anchor="middle" font-size="28" fill="#6B7280" font-weight="800" font-family="sans-serif">~60%</text>
            <text x="245" y="365" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" fill="#374151" font-weight="600" font-family="sans-serif">GPT-3.5</text>
            <text x="245" y="385" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#6B7280" font-family="sans-serif">USMLE</text>
            <!-- Med-PaLM 2 bar (86.5%) -->
            <rect x="370" y="91" width="110" height="247" fill="url(#g2)" rx="6"/>
            <text x="425" y="77" text-anchor="middle" font-size="28" fill="#3D7A8A" font-weight="800" font-family="sans-serif">86.5%</text>
            <text x="425" y="365" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" fill="#374151" font-weight="600" font-family="sans-serif">Med-PaLM 2</text>
            <text x="425" y="385" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#6B7280" font-family="sans-serif">MedQA</text>
            <!-- GPT-4 bar (>90%) -->
            <rect x="550" y="80" width="110" height="258" fill="url(#g3)" rx="6"/>
            <text x="605" y="66" text-anchor="middle" font-size="28" fill="#1B2A4A" font-weight="800" font-family="sans-serif">&gt;90%</text>
            <text x="605" y="365" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" fill="#374151" font-weight="600" font-family="sans-serif">GPT-4</text>
            <text x="605" y="385" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#6B7280" font-family="sans-serif">USMLE</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="perf-text">
          <p>LLM performance on standardized medical examinations has demonstrated rapid improvement across model generations, though real-world clinical performance remains less well characterized.</p>
          <div class="perf-highlight">
            <div class="ph-value">&gt;90%</div>
            <div class="ph-label">GPT-4 on all three USMLE steps, substantially exceeding the ~60% passing threshold</div>
          </div>
          <div class="perf-highlight">
            <div class="ph-value">86.5%</div>
            <div class="ph-label">Med-PaLM 2 on MedQA, approaching expert physician-level performance</div>
          </div>
          <p>Earlier models such as GPT-3.5 scored near the passing threshold but fell short on complex clinical reasoning tasks.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- RISKS -->
    <div class="risks-section">
      <h2>Risks, Limitations, &amp; Ethical Concerns</h2>
      <p class="risks-subtitle">Despite impressive benchmarks, significant concerns persist that must be addressed before safe clinical deployment.</p>
      <div class="risks-grid">
        <div class="risk-card">
          <div class="risk-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2L1 21h22L12 2zm0 4l7.53 13H4.47L12 6zm-1 5v4h2v-4h-2zm0 6v2h2v-2h-2z"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Hallucinations</h3>
          <p>LLMs fabricate plausible-sounding but incorrect medical information, including fake citations and invented clinical references.</p>
          <div class="risk-stat">Up to 30%<span>hallucination rate in medical Q&amp;A</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="risk-card">
          <div class="risk-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 12c2.21 0 4-1.79 4-4s-1.79-4-4-4-4 1.79-4 4 1.79 4 4 4zm0 2c-2.67 0-8 1.34-8 4v2h16v-2c0-2.66-5.33-4-8-4z"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Bias &amp; Equity</h3>
          <p>Models may perpetuate or amplify biases present in training data, leading to disparities in care recommendations across demographic groups.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="risk-card">
          <div class="risk-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M18 8h-1V6c0-2.76-2.24-5-5-5S7 3.24 7 6v2H6c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v10c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h12c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V10c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2zm-6 9c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2s.9-2 2-2 2 .9 2 2-.9 2-2 2zm3.1-9H8.9V6c0-1.71 1.39-3.1 3.1-3.1s3.1 1.39 3.1 3.1v2z"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Privacy</h3>
          <p>Patient data used in prompts may be transmitted to external servers, raising serious HIPAA and GDPR compliance concerns.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="risks-grid-bottom">
        <div class="risk-card">
          <div class="risk-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 16.17L4.83 12l-1.42 1.41L9 19 21 7l-1.41-1.41L9 16.17z"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Lack of Clinical Validation</h3>
          <p>Most LLM evaluations rely on multiple-choice benchmarks rather than prospective clinical trials, creating a gap between test performance and real-world applicability.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="risk-card">
          <div class="risk-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2C6.48 2 2 6.48 2 12s4.48 10 10 10 10-4.48 10-10S17.52 2 12 2zm-2 15l-5-5 1.41-1.41L10 14.17l7.59-7.59L19 8l-9 9z"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Over-reliance Risk</h3>
          <p>Clinicians may develop automation bias, accepting LLM outputs without sufficient critical appraisal, especially under time pressure.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- FRAMEWORK -->
    <div class="framework-section">
      <h2>A Framework for Responsible Deployment</h2>
      <div class="framework-steps">
        <div class="framework-step">
          <div class="step-circle">1</div>
          <h3>Rigorous Prospective Evaluation</h3>
          <p>In diverse clinical settings before deployment</p>
        </div>
        <div class="framework-step">
          <div class="step-circle">2</div>
          <h3>Human-in-the-Loop Design</h3>
          <p>Ensuring clinician oversight of all LLM-generated outputs</p>
        </div>
        <div class="framework-step">
          <div class="step-circle">3</div>
          <h3>Transparent Reporting</h3>
          <p>Of model limitations, training data, and known failure modes</p>
        </div>
        <div class="framework-step">
          <div class="step-circle">4</div>
          <h3>Equity Audits</h3>
          <p>Assessing differential performance across patient populations</p>
        </div>
        <div class="framework-step">
          <div class="step-circle">5</div>
          <h3>Regulatory Alignment</h3>
          <p>With evolving FDA, EMA, and WHO guidance on AI medical devices</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CONSENSUS -->
    <div class="consensus-banner">
      <p>LLMs hold <strong>transformative potential</strong> for medicine, but their deployment must be guided by <strong>evidence, equity, and robust governance</strong> to ensure patient safety.</p>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- FOOTER -->
  <div class="footer">
    <div class="ref-text">
      Based on: &ldquo;Large language models in medicine&rdquo; &mdash; Nature Medicine, July 2023 &nbsp;|&nbsp; USMLE: Kung et al., 2023; Med-PaLM 2: Singhal et al., 2023 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Hallucination rates: multiple studies, 2023
    </div>
    <div class="venue-badge">Medical AI &amp; Digital Health 2024</div>
  </div>

</div>
</body>
</html>
