 2 bar (86.5%) -->", "+            <rect x="370" y="91" width="110" height="247" fill="url(#g2)" rx="6"/>", "+            <text x="425" y="77" text-anchor="middle" font-size="28" fill="#3D7A8A" font-weight="800" font-family="sans-serif">86.5%</text>", "+            <text x="425" y="365" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" fill="#374151" font-weight="600" font-family="sans-serif">Med-PaLM 2</text>", "+            <text x="425" y="385" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#6B7280" font-family="sans-serif">MedQA</text>", "+            <!-- GPT-4 bar (>90%) -->", "+            <rect x="550" y="80" width="110" height="258" fill="url(#g3)" rx="6"/>", "+            <text x="605" y="66" text-anchor="middle" font-size="28" fill="#1B2A4A" font-weight="800" font-family="sans-serif">&gt;90%</text>", "+            <text x="605" y="365" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" fill="#374151" font-weight="600" font-family="sans-serif">GPT-4</text>", "+            <text x="605" y="385" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#6B7280" font-family="sans-serif">USMLE</text>", "           </svg>", "         </div>", "         <div class="perf-text">", "-          <p>LLM performance on standardized medical examinations has been a key area of evaluation, demonstrating rapid improvement across model generations.</p>", "+          <p>LLM performance on standardized medical examinations has demonstrated rapid improvement across model generations, though real-world clinical performance remains less well characterized.</p>", "           <div class="perf-highlight">", "             <div class="ph-value">&gt;90%</div>", "             <div class="ph-label">GPT-4 on all three USMLE steps, substantially exceeding the ~60% passing threshold</div>"]}, {"oldStart": 623, "oldLines": 39, "newStart": 515, "newLines": 43, "lines": ["             <div class="ph-value">86.5%</div>", "             <div class="ph-label">Med-PaLM 2 on MedQA, approaching expert physician-level performance</div>", "           </div>", "-          <p>These results suggest LLMs encode substantial medical knowledge, though performance on real-world clinical scenarios remains less well characterized.</p>", "+          <p>Earlier models such as GPT-3.5 scored near the passing threshold but fell short on complex clinical reasoning tasks.</p>", "         </div>", "       </div>", "     </div>", " ", "-    <!-- RISKS & LIMITATIONS -->", "+    <!-- RISKS -->", "     <div class="risks-section">", "       <h2>Risks, Limitations, &amp; Ethical Concerns</h2>", "+      <p class="risks-subtitle">Despite impressive benchmarks, significant concerns persist that must be addressed before safe clinical deployment.</p>", "       <div class="risks-grid">", "         <div class="risk-card">", "-          <div class="risk-number">1</div>", "+          <div class="risk-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2L1 21h22L12 2zm0 4l7.53 13H4.47L12 6zm-1 5v4h2v-4h-2zm0 6v2h2v-2h-2z"/></svg></div>", "           <h3>Hallucinations</h3>", "-          <p>LLMs fabricate plausible-sounding but incorrect medical information, including fake citations. Rates up to 30% in medical Q&amp;A tasks.</p>", "+          <p>LLMs fabricate plausible-sounding but incorrect medical information, including fake citations and invented clinical references.</p>", "+          <div class="risk-stat">Up to 30%<span>hallucination rate in medical Q&amp;A</span></div>", "         </div>", "         <div class="risk-card">", "-          <div class="risk-number">2</div>", "+          <div class="risk-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 12c2.21 0 4-1.79 4-4s-1.79-4-4-4-4 1.79-4 4 1.79 4 4 4zm0 2c-2.67 0-8 1.34-8 4v2h16v-2c0-2.66-5.33-4-8-4z"/></svg></div>", "           <h3>Bias &amp; Equity</h3>", "-          <p>Models may perpetuate or amplify biases in training data, leading to disparities in care recommendations across demographic groups.</p>", "+          <p>Models may perpetuate or amplify biases present in training data, leading to disparities in care recommendations across demographic groups.</p>", "         </div>", "         <div class="risk-card">", "-          <div class="risk-number">3</div>", "+          <div class="risk-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M18 8h-1V6c0-2.76-2.24-5-5-5S7 3.24 7 6v2H6c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v10c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h12c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V10c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2zm-6 9c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2s.9-2 2-2 2 .9 2 2-.9 2-2 2zm3.1-9H8.9V6c0-1.71 1.39-3.1 3.1-3.1s3.1 1.39 3.1 3.1v2z"/></svg></div>", "           <h3>Privacy</h3>", "-          <p>Patient data in prompts may be transmitted to external servers, raising serious HIPAA and GDPR compliance concerns.</p>", "+          <p>Patient data used in prompts may be transmitted to external servers, raising serious HIPAA and GDPR compliance concerns.</p>", "         </div>", "+      </div>", "+      <div class="risks-grid-bottom">", "         <div class="risk-card">", "-          <div class="risk-number">4</div>", "+          <div class="risk-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 16.17L4.83 12l-1.42 1.41L9 19 21 7l-1.41-1.41L9 16.17z"/></svg></div>", "           <h3>Lack of Clinical Validation</h3>", "-          <p>Most LLM evaluations rely on multiple-choice benchmarks rather than prospective clinical trials.</p>", "+          <p>Most LLM evaluations rely on multiple-choice benchmarks rather than prospective clinical trials, creating a gap between test performance and real-world applicability.</p>", "         </div>", "         <div class="risk-card">", "-          <div class="risk-number">5</div>", "+          <div class="risk-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2C6.48 2 2 6.48 2 12s4.48 10 10 10 10-4.48 10-10S17.52 2 12 2zm-2 15l-5-5 1.41-1.41L10 14.17l7.59-7.59L19 8l-9 9z"/></svg></div>", "           <h3>Over-reliance Risk</h3>", "-          <p>Clinicians may develop automation bias, accepting LLM outputs without sufficient critical appraisal.</p>", "+          <p>Clinicians may develop automation bias, accepting LLM outputs without sufficient critical appraisal, especially under time pressure.</p>", "         </div>", "       </div>", "     </div>"]}, {"oldStart": 677, "oldLines": 22, "newStart": 573, "newLines": 22, "lines": ["         <div class="framework-step">", "           <div class="step-circle">3</div>", "           <h3>Transparent Reporting</h3>", "-          <p>Of model limitations, training data sources, and known failure modes</p>", "+          <p>Of model limitations, training data, and known failure modes</p>", "         </div>", "         <div class="framework-step">", "           <div class="step-circle">4</div>", "           <h3>Equity Audits</h3>", "-          <p>To assess differential performance across patient populations</p>", "+          <p>Assessing differential performance across patient populations</p>", "         </div>", "         <div class="framework-step">", "           <div class="step-circle">5</div>", "           <h3>Regulatory Alignment</h3>", "-          <p>With evolving FDA, EMA, and WHO guidance on AI-based medical devices</p>", "+          <p>With evolving FDA, EMA, and WHO guidance on AI medical devices</p>", "         </div>", "       </div>", "     </div>", " ", "-    <!-- CONSENSUS BANNER -->", "+    <!-- CONSENSUS -->", "     <div class="consensus-banner">", "       <p>LLMs hold <strong>transformative potential</strong> for medicine, but their deployment must be guided by <strong>evidence, equity, and robust governance</strong> to ensure patient safety.</p>", "     </div>"]}, {"oldStart": 702, "oldLines": 7, "newStart": 598, "newLines": 7, "lines": ["   <!-- FOOTER -->", "   <div class="footer">", "     <div class="ref-text">", "-      Based on: &ldquo;Large language models in medicine&rdquo; &mdash; Nature Medicine, July 2023. &nbsp;|&nbsp; USMLE data: Kung et al., 2023; Med-PaLM 2: Singhal et al., 2023. &nbsp;|&nbsp; Hallucination rates: multiple studies, 2023.", "+      Based on: &ldquo;Large language models in medicine&rdquo; &mdash; Nature Med